From c92da3f9bdd8b94f89f894bf872e82ed7c3d0ec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:10:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] [flutter_tools] Add the linux_ppc64 host and target
 platform

Class: upstreamable in form (it follows flutter#178711, the linux_riscv64
tool enablement merged for 3.44, shape for shape); local until the Dart
VM has an upstream ppc64 backend, which upstream policy rules out.

Names, as fixed for the port: HostPlatform.linux_ppc64 and
TargetPlatform.linux_ppc64; `linux-ppc64` for --target-platform, cache
and engine artifact directories (`linux-ppc64`, `linux-ppc64-profile`,
`linux-ppc64-release`); `ppc64` for the CMake build directory
(build/linux/ppc64/<mode>/bundle), FLUTTER_HOST_ARCH and the
native-assets Architecture.

* os.dart: the enum value, platformName `ppc64`, `linux-ppc64`, and the
  `linux_ppc64` ABI name and `ppc64` FLUTTER_HOST_ARCH value.
* build_info.dart: the enum value, osName `linux`, simpleName `ppc64`,
  and the `linux-ppc64` name in both directions.
* artifacts.dart: desktop artifact paths, the host target for a
  linux_ppc64 host, the `linux-ppc64` prebuilt directory of a local
  engine, and `clang_ppc64` among the local-engine gen_snapshot dirs.
* build linux: `linux-ppc64` is allowed and is the default on a ppc64
  host. The old check rejected every non-arm64 target on a non-x64
  host, so it is now the cross-build check of #178711; building for
  ppc64 on any other host is refused, since gen_snapshot for ppc64 is
  only built as a ppc64 binary.
* assemble: debug/profile/release Linux bundle targets for linux_ppc64.
* Linux device, AOT platform list, kernel snapshot, shader compiler,
  application package, mdns, resident runner, artifact selection and
  Android switch arms, as #178711 does for riscv64.
* native assets: linux_ppc64 builds hooks for (OS.linux,
  Architecture.ppc64), and ppc64 is a Linux architecture. This needs
  the vendored code_assets of the previous commit.
* bin/internal/update_dart_sdk.sh: `uname -m` ppc64le selects the
  `linux-ppc64` Dart SDK name instead of falling back to arm64.

Not taken from #178711: the riscv64 feature flag (it gates
cross-building, which ppc64 does not support at all) and the extra
Fuchsia debug-symbol download.

Tests mirror #178711 and cover each new name and mapping: build_linux
(debug, profile, release with --analyze-size under build/linux/ppc64,
and the three cross-build refusals), os, build_info, artifacts, cache
(font-subset, FlutterSdk and Linux engine dirs), linux_device, Linux
bundle target names, plugin registrant, and native-assets targets
(including the `ppc64` target_architecture in the hook input).
